# Geo Core release (agents)

When shipping **reactwoo-geocore**, follow `docs/releases-and-git-tags.md` §2.

## Required pattern

1. `git commit` — standalone command.
2. `git tag -a "vVERSION" -m "…"` — **standalone** command (never chained with push on Windows).
3. `git push origin main "vVERSION"` — **one** push, not `push main` then `push tag`.

Use SSH push on Windows (see `.cursor/rules/git-push-windows.mdc`):

```bash
GIT_SSH_COMMAND="ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=15" git push origin main "vVERSION"
```

## Do not

- Chain `commit && tag && archive && push && push` in one line.
- Run two pushes to origin unless the combined push failed and you are retrying only the missing ref.
- Run local `git archive` before tag push unless the user needs a zip before CI (tag push runs `publish-update.yml`).

## If push/tag fails with exit 139 or fork errors

Retry **only** the failed step in a new shell command (e.g. tag alone, then `git push origin main "vVERSION"`).
